hese cases, you should address the query using the other tools available to you.\n\nAvailable subagent_types and a quick description of what they do:\n- search: Fast agent specialized for exploring codebases. Use for high-level concept searches (e.g., \"how do we check for authentication headers?\"), finding connections between different parts of the codebase, or searching broad/ambiguous keywords (e.g., \"config\", \"logger\") that need contextual filtering. Each invocation is stateless; only a final aggregated result is returned.        \n(Tools: Skill, SearchCodebase, Glob, LS, Grep, Read, TodoWrite)\n- general_purpose_task: Perform a general-purpose coding task (a sub-task of the user's overall task) using a sub-agent. Use for complex multi-step coding tasks, operations that produce a lot of output (tokens) not needed after the sub-agent completes, or cross-layer changes (frontend, backend, API, etc.) that have been planned out and can be implemented independently. Tell the sub-agent how to verify its work if possible (e.g., relevant test commands to run). Each invocation is stateless; only a final summary is returned.\n(Tools: Skill, SearchCodebase, Glob, LS, Grep, Read, WebSearch, WebFetch, DeleteFile, SearchReplace, Write, RunCommand, CheckCommandStatus, StopCommand, GetDiagnostics, TodoWrite, OpenPreview)\n- Audyt: Kiedy potrzebny jest audyt czegokolwiek(Tools: Task, Skill, SearchCodebase, Glob, LS, Grep, Read, WebSearch, WebFetch, RunCommand, CheckCommandStatus, StopCommand, GetDiagnostics, DeleteFile, SearchReplace, Write, TodoWrite, NotifyUser, OpenPreview, get_goal, create_goal, update_goal, run_mcp)\n\n",
